  "verbalization": "Cinnabaramide C is implicated in the regulation of WRL68 through a series of molecular interactions involving the enzyme Peptide deformylase. This enzyme is a target of Cinnabaramide C and is also a target of two other compounds, Npc158230 and Phyllaemblicin D, all of which ultimately lead to the activation of WRL68. The observed scores suggest a consistent and significant relationship between Cinnabaramide C and WRL68, with the pathway involving Peptide deformylase acting as a critical mediator. The mechanism likely involves the inhibition of Peptide deformylase, which in turn affects the downstream signaling cascade leading to WRL68 activation. The integration of multiple pathways supports a plausible mechanism where Cinnabaramide C exerts its effect through the modulation of Peptide deformylase, which is a key player in the regulation of WRL68. The evidence is robust and consistent, reinforcing the hypothesis that Cinnabaramide C interacts with WRL68 via this enzymatic pathway.",
